@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

#
# prima-materia — the searches of the run on the Ājīvika transmission,
# 2026-10-07
#
# In a file of their own for the mechanical reason recorded at
# examinations/searches-jain.ttl and in prima-materia#703.
#
# Three searches. The first is the one this holding exists to make and it came
# back empty in a way that is itself the finding: the transmission asserts
# that nothing a person does alters anything, so there is no capacity claim to
# find. The second mapped how far the sole witness is from the thing it
# reports. The third is the one that should have been cheap and was not.
#

pmp:AjivikaYieldingSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether any source reports the Ājīvikas asserting a capacity reached by practice"@en, "Ob eine Quelle berichtet, die Ājīvikas hätten ein durch Übung erreichbares Vermögen behauptet"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Every place in the Pali canon that names the bamboo-staffed ascetic Gosāla or the Ājīvaka ascetics, located by a search of the whole canon and read in the Pali of the Mahāsaṅgīti Tipiṭaka Buddhavasse 2500 with the English of Bhikkhu Sujato: seventeen places for the name of the teacher and thirty for the name of the ascetics, of which the doctrinal ones are Dīgha Nikāya 2, Saṁyutta Nikāya 24.8, Aṅguttara Nikāya 3.137 and 6.57, and Majjhima Nikāya 76; the rest are monastic-rule passages, verses and name lists."@en ;
    pm:searchedFor "The form of claim this holding collects: a practice, however described, that the transmission is reported to have held brings about a state, a power or an attainment. The question is put to this transmission because its own registration called it the limiting case and because the structure-driven entrance sends a run to places nobody asked about."@en ;
    pm:searchTerms "In the Pali: iddhi, abhiññā, tapa, tapas, brahmacariya, sīla, vata, paripācessāmi, byantiṁ karissāmi, vīriya, purisaparakkama, attakāra, parakāra; and the names makkhali, gosāla, ājīvaka, ājīvika in every spelling the canon uses, each hit opened in its sutta."@en ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundNothing ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-07" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-07" ;
    skos:note "Nothing, and the nothing is a doctrine and not a gap. The passages found say the opposite in the plainest words the canon has: there is no cause and no condition for the purification of beings, no act of one's own and none of another, no power, no energy, no human strength, no human exertion; and there is no such thing as by this precept or vow or austerity or holy life I shall ripen an unripe deed or wear away a ripe one. Node pmc:AjivikaNaTapasaParipaka. The Aṅguttara's own summary of the doctrine is three words long and is the same: natthi kammaṁ, natthi kiriyaṁ, natthi vīriyaṁ."@en ;
    skos:note "So traditions/ajivika.ttl carries no pm:Yielding and cannot. That is the only file in this holding of which that is true for a reason rather than for want of reading, and the reason is worth more to the project than a capacity would have been: the holding now has one registered transmission whose reported position is the denial of every other transmission in it."@en ;
    skos:note "What was found instead and is not a capacity: an end that arrives without being reached. Fools and the wise alike make an end of suffering after running through the enumerated round, as a thrown ball of thread runs on only while it unwinds. Nodes pmc:AjivikaSamsarasuddhi and pmc:AjivikaSuttagulaUpama. A later run must not read that as an attainment; the text makes it independent of anything anybody does."@en .

pmp:AjivikaWitnessSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the sole witness keeps the doctrine attached to one teacher"@en, "Ob der einzige Zeuge die Lehre bei einem Lehrer hält"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "The same places in the same edition, with the three doctrinal blocks read in the Pali side by side: Dīgha Nikāya 2 at the headings Makkhaligosālavāda and Pakudhakaccāyanavāda, Saṁyutta Nikāya 24.8, and Aṅguttara Nikāya 6.57."@en ;
    pm:searchedFor "Whether the enumeration and the denial of austerity that the Sāmaññaphalasutta ascribes to Makkhali Gosāla stand elsewhere in the same canon, and under whose name. This is the counter-search to every ascription in traditions/ajivika.ttl: a report whose own canon moves the doctrine between teachers is a weaker witness than one that does not, and that has to be established before the ascriptions are written and not after."@en ;
    pm:searchTerms "The shared clauses themselves rather than keywords: niyatisaṅgatibhāvapariṇatā, cuddasa yonipamukhasatasahassāni, aparipakkaṁ kammaṁ paripācessāmi, suttaguḷe khitte, sattime kāyā akaṭā akaṭavidhā, chaḷābhijātiyo; each sought across the canon and each occurrence read with the heading above it."@en ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundOpposing ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:AjivikaAnattributaDitthi, pmc:AjivikaChalabhijati, pmc:AjivikaChalabhijatiVivada ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-07" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-07" ;
    skos:note "It does not. Three places and three arrangements. The Sāmaññaphalasutta gives the enumeration with the ball of thread to Makkhali Gosāla and the seven unmade bodies with the sword that takes no life to Pakudha Kaccāyana, in two separate sections six paragraphs apart. The Mahādiṭṭhisutta runs both together as one view and names no teacher for it. The Chaḷabhijātisutta gives the six classes of birth, which the Sāmaññaphalasutta has inside Makkhali's own enumeration, to Pūraṇa Kassapa, and has Gosāla appear in that scheme as a member of its highest class instead of as its author."@en ;
    skos:note "Recorded as opposing material and not as a find, because what it opposes is the holding's own ascriptions. It does not show the doctrine false and it does not show it not Ājīvika; it shows that the one canon this transmission is reached through does not treat these blocks as the property of one teacher. Every node of traditions/ajivika.ttl carries pm:thirdPartyAscription for that reason, and the dispute itself is entered at pmc:AjivikaChalabhijatiVivada rather than left in this note."@en ;
    skos:note "The witness's stance, from the same search and from the same canon: the Kesakambalasutta calls this doctrine the worst of all the doctrines of ascetics and brahmins and its teacher a trap for humans. A hostile witness that also shuffles the material between teachers is the weakest kind of source this holding admits, and it is the only kind available here."@en .

pmp:AjivikaSelfWitnessSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether anything the Ājīvikas themselves produced is reachable"@en, "Ob irgendetwas von den Ājīvikas selbst erreichbar ist"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Not a corpus but the question of whether one exists: the search was for a text, an inscription or a documentary record transmitted by the Ājīvikas themselves rather than by their opponents, the registration of this transmission having asserted that there is none."@en ;
    pm:searchedFor "A self-witness of any kind, against which the ascriptions of this file could be checked. Without one, every node of traditions/ajivika.ttl rests on a canon that is hostile to it, and the holding cannot distinguish the doctrine from the report of the doctrine."@en ;
    pm:searchTerms "Ājīvika, Ājīvaka, Āgīvika, Ājīvikas with the terms text, canon, scripture, inscription, surviving, lost; the names Nanda Vaccha, Kisa Saṅkicca, Makkhali Gosāla, Maskarin Gośāliputra; and the Tamil and Sanskrit forms of the name."@en ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundNothing ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-07" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-07" ;
    skos:note "The search was carried at the first of the two stages only, and that is stated rather than glossed over: it established that no transmitted work of the Ājīvikas is named as reachable, and it did not open a second-hand account to confirm it, because the standard study of the transmission could not be reached on the day of the run. That is a property of the access path and not of the work: archive.org, which is the regular route of this holding and carries that study, answered every request of this run with a global outage page. The reading this file does rest on did not need it; the claim that nothing of their own survives still does."@en ;
    skos:note "So the registration's sentence that this transmission has no corpus of its own stands unconfirmed by this run, and is the one thing in this file that a reader should not take on its authority. The next run on this transmission can settle it in one reading, and the place to go is named in AGENTS.md once archive.org answers again."@en .
